{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "integral_column_midpoint",
    "description": "MMS driver for the five `integral` lowerings on grids/column_nonuniform_1d, one model per form (the convergence runner takes one L2_error assertion per model): FromBottomCenter (integral_lev_cumulative_from_bottom, upper bound `lev`), ToTopCenter (integral_lev_cumulative_to_top, lower bound `lev`), FromBottomNodes (integral_lev_nodes_cumulative_from_bottom, upper bound `lev_nodes`), ToTopNodes (integral_lev_nodes_cumulative_to_top, lower bound `lev_nodes`) and Whole (integral_lev_whole, both bounds constants). The integrand is the state-free layer field f = 1 + cos(pi z) sampled at the layer centres of the quadratic-stretch column z(xi) = 0.6 xi + 0.4 xi^2, whose antiderivative z + sin(pi z)/pi gives every form in closed form (whole column = 1). Each model carries an accumulator state (w_fbc, w_ttc, w_fbn, w_ttn, w_whole -- one distinct name per model, so sibling models never share a state name) with ic 0 and d/dt = F, so its value at t = 1 equals the lowered integral F exactly whatever the integrator does (the right-hand side is constant in time), and the L2 error of w against the analytic integral -- evaluated at the layer centres for the centre forms and at the interfaces for the node forms -- isolates the midpoint-rule error, which is second order on the smoothly stretched mesh. The mesh follows the grid's edge-array contract (ze supplied; zc, dz grid-derived); the references spell the layer centre or interface coordinate from literals and NLEV (build-time scope caveat).",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:problem",
      "grid:column_nonuniform_1d",
      "equation:integral",
      "mms"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Roache, P. J. (2002). Code verification by the method of manufactured solutions. J. Fluids Eng. 124(1), 4-10.",
        "doi": "10.1115/1.1436090"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Davis, P. J. and Rabinowitz, P. (1984). Methods of Numerical Integration, 2nd ed. Academic Press. Section 2.1 (midpoint rule)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "FromBottomCenter": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../grids/column_nonuniform_1d/rules/integral_lev_cumulative_from_bottom.esm"
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "f": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/m",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Integrand 1 + cos(pi zc[i]) sampled at the layer centres (state-free), spelled as an explicit gather over lev so every binding's evaluator binds the layer-centre array inside the aggregate scope."
        },
        "F": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "The lowered integral: cumulative integral from the surface to the layer centre, z + sin(pi z)/pi at z = zc."
        },
        "zbot": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Surface coordinate, the constant lower bound of the integral (measure-free documentation per esm-spec 4.2)."
        },
        "ztop": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "Top coordinate, the constant upper bound of the integral."
        },
        "ze": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "shape": [
            "lev_nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Interface coordinates of the quadratic-stretch column, ze[kn] = 0.6 ((kn-1)/NLEV) + 0.4 ((kn-1)/NLEV)^2 for kn = 1..NLEV+1 (ze[1] = 0 the surface, ze[NLEV+1] = 1 the top): the single geometry input of the grid's edge-array contract, spelled from the metaparameter name NLEV so a loader-API rebinding re-derives the whole mesh."
        },
        "zc": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Layer centres, GRID-DERIVED from ze by applying grids/column_nonuniform_1d column_cell_center. Read by the rules by bare name."
        },
        "dz": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Layer thicknesses, GRID-DERIVED from ze by applying column_cell_thickness. The finite-volume measure read by the rules by bare name."
        },
        "w_fbc": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Accumulator state with ic 0 and dw_fbc/dt = F, so w_fbc(1) = F exactly for every integrator (the integrand of the ODE is constant in time) and the L2 error of w at t = 1 against the analytic integral is the error of the midpoint-rule lowering alone."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": {
            "op": "ic",
            "args": [
              "w_fbc"
            ]
          },
          "rhs": 0.0
        },
        {
          "lhs": {
            "op": "D",
            "args": [
              "w_fbc"
            ],
            "wrt": "t"
          },
          "rhs": "F"
        },
        {
          "lhs": "f",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "i"
            ],
            "args": [
              "zc"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "i": {
                "from": "lev"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "+",
              "args": [
                1.0,
                {
                  "op": "cos",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        3.141592653589793,
                        {
                          "op": "index",
                          "args": [
                            "zc",
                            "i"
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "F",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "integral",
            "args": [
              "f"
            ],
            "var": "lev",
            "lower": "zbot",
            "upper": "lev"
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "ze",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "kn"
            ],
            "args": [],
            "ranges": {
              "kn": {
                "from": "lev_nodes"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "+",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "*",
                  "args": [
                    0.6,
                    {
                      "op": "/",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "-",
                          "args": [
                            "kn",
                            1
                          ]
                        },
                        "NLEV"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "*",
                  "args": [
                    0.4,
                    {
                      "op": "/",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "-",
                          "args": [
                            "kn",
                            1
                          ]
                        },
                        "NLEV"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "/",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "-",
                          "args": [
                            "kn",
                            1
                          ]
                        },
                        "NLEV"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "zc",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "column_cell_center",
            "bindings": {
              "ze": "ze"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "dz",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "column_cell_thickness",
            "bindings": {
              "ze": "ze"
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "midpoint_center_from_bottom",
          "description": "w_fbc(1) = F, the midpoint-rule lowering of the integral of 1 + cos(pi z) on the quadratic-stretch column, compared in L2 against the analytic cumulative integral from the surface to the layer centre, z + sin(pi z)/pi at z = zc. at the default NLEV = 64 (second-order; per-resolution errors pinned in tests/conformance/convergence/integral_column_center_from_bottom/golden/errors.json).",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 1.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "w_fbc",
              "time": 1.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": {
                "abs": 0.0001
